can, so the expected margin stays modest and uncertainty is wide.", "watch": "Republicans consolidating behind Treg Taylor, whether through dropouts or ranked-choice transfers, is the most likely path back to a genuine toss-up.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mike Dunleavy (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Alaska's governorship is open for the first time in a decade with Mike Dunleavy term-limited. Democrat Jonathan Kreiss-Tomkins faces three Republicans, Treg Taylor, Bernadette Wilson and Dave Bronson, under the state's ranked-choice system. Kreiss-Tomkins has raised about $2.2 million, well ahead of Taylor's $880,000, and the GOP side has been marked by infighting, with Wilson pressing rivals to drop out and party figures divided over whether to 'rank the red.'\n\nA September poll from a Republican-leaning firm put Kreiss-Tomkins up three points, though large swaths of voters remain undecided. Most race raters call it a toss-up, but prediction markets price the Democrat near 75 percent and one rater rates it a safe Democratic flip. The state's Republican lean and the chance that ranked-choice transfers consolidate GOP support keep the outcome genuinely uncertain.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6825, "margin": 2.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7335, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7395, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7331, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7068, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7071, "margin": 3.5}]}